      "content": "that sounds good in theory but it's hard to do in practice. parents in our district are really split. some say focusing on the \"complex aspects\" just makes kids feel guilty or divided, while others say ignoring the systemic stuff is basically lying to them about how the world works. if you had to pick one to prioritize as the foundation so kids actually learn how to be informed citizens, which way do you think is more logically sound?",
